url: "https://github.com/kavan010/black_hole"
version: "0.8.0"
abstract: >-
  C++17/OpenGL 4.3 realtime null-geodesic visualization of a Schwarzschild
  black hole at Sagittarius A* scale, with a Blender 4.x addon frontend.
  The default path preserves the historical visual/physics baseline
  (single-stage Euler compute shader). Opt-in additions: a GPU scientific
  mode (pole-safe planar RK4, continuous hit tests, derived escape criterion,
  Doppler and gravitational redshift), a deterministic double-precision CPU
  reference renderer (Page-Thorne thin-disk blackbody emission, RK4/RK45)
  validated against the GPU, and a Blender render bridge. Kerr is provided
  only as closed-form analytic radii; no Kerr ray tracing, radiative
  transfer or GRMHD.
keywords:
  - black-hole
  - gravitational-lensing
  - geodesic
